## Installing this package as a developer (updated).

1. Install [rust](https://rust-lang.org/tools/install/), we want to use `uv` (package manager), `mdbook` (documentation), and `mdbook-cmdrun` (dynamic documentation).

- Disconnect from SRN to install rust.
- run `cargo install uv`, `cargo install mdbook`, `cargo install mdbook-cmdrun` after rust is installed.
- To use `uv`, `export UV_NATIVE_TLS=true`

2. Create and activate virtual enviroment: `uv venv` (will default to a .venv directory).

```
source .venv/bin/activate       # for bash shell
source .venv/bin/activate.csh   # for c shell
source .venv/bin/activate.fish  # for fish shell
.\.venv\Scripts\activate        # for powershell
```

3. Install module dependencies: `uv pip install -e .[dev]` (add `--trusted-host pypi.python.org --trusted-host pypi.org --trusted-host files.pythonhosted.org` if there are issues, also disconnect from SRN if there are errors).
4. Verify installation was successful: `precon3d` should show:

```

        +-------------+
       /             /|
      /             / |
     +-------------+  |    PRECON3D:
     |   slice 1   |  |    (PRE)pare and re(CON)struct
     |      2      |  |    serial sectioning montage data
     |      3      |  |    into 3D volume 🧊
     |     ...     |  +
     |   slice n   | /
     +-------------+/


Usage: precon3d [MODULE] [COMMAND] [PARAMETERS]

PRECON3D: (PRE)pare and re(CON)struct serial sectioning montage data into 3D volume 🧊

 Module              Short help
 czi_info            Access information about the CZI file.
 shading_correction  Estimate shading correction from tiles
 stitcher_fiji       Stitch TilesArrays from czi
 stitcher            Stitch TileRegions from czi
 pol_prep            Prepare polarized images
 aligner             Image registration/alignment methods
 cropper             Crop images to regions of interest
 downscaler          Downscale images
 resampler           Resample slices
 utility             Utilities for file management

```

## Installing a package (depracated).

- setup your git keys
- install python to make sure you have a working version

```bash
python --version
python3 --version
python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip setuptools #global upgrade
```

- setup proxy stuff
- create virtual environment

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv #make venv
```

- activate the environment

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate       # for bash shell
source .venv/bin/activate.csh   # for c shell
source .venv/bin/activate.fish  # for fish shell
.\.venv\Scripts\activate        # for powershell
```

- install the package with pip

```bash
pip install -e .[dev]  # install in dev mode, with editable
```

## Package Notes

- src structure: https://www.pyopensci.org/python-package-guide/package-structure-code/python-package-structure.html
- test coverage

```bash
pytest --cov=src --cov-report=xml:coverage_reports/coverage.xml --cov-report=html:coverage_reports/htmlcov --cov-report=term tests/
```

- mdbook

```sh
mdbook serve ./docs/userguide/ --open # server view
mdbook build ./docs/userguide/        # build the book
```

## Project layout

    mkdocs.yml    # The configuration file.
    docs/
        index.md  # The documentation homepage.
        ...       # Other markdown pages, images and other files.

- api docs

```bash
env:
  PROJECT_NAME: python_template
echo "Project Name: $PROJECT_NAME"
pdoc ./src/$PROJECT_NAME/  -o ./docs/api
pdoc ./src/python_template/  -o ./docs/api
```
